      "id": "embeddings-retrieval-1",
      "document_id": "embeddings-retrieval",
      "title": "Embeddings and Retrieval",
      "section": "Similarity and top-k",
      "text": " Cosine similarity compares the angle between a query vector and a chunk vector, which makes it useful when text length varies. Top-k retrieval returns a small set of the highest-scoring chunks; increasing k can improve recall but also adds noise to the prompt. Scores should be logged so weak retrieval can be diagnosed.  ",
