      "document_id": "python-foundations",
      "title": "Python Foundations",
      "section": "Functions and single responsibility",
      "text": " A Python function should have one clear responsibility and a name that explains the action it performs. Keep inputs explicit, return a value rather than changing unrelated global state, and document surprising behavior. Small functions are easier to test because each one has fewer paths and dependencies.  ",
