      "title": "Python Foundations",
      "section": "Choosing data structures",
      "text": " Use a list for ordered collections, a tuple for a fixed record, a set for membership checks, and a dictionary for key-value lookup. Choosing the structure that matches the question makes code easier to read and usually improves performance. Prefer comprehensions for simple transformations, but use a loop when the logic needs multiple steps.  ",
